{#- Official Go shared-enums template (design §22 G2).
    Registered under the target's `enums_file` name and rendered once,
    only when the schema has at least one non-empty enum. `emitted_enums`
    is precomputed in context (name order; `name` the schema banner name,
    `ident` the package-level allocated type, `backing` the type literal,
    `const_lines` the gofmt-aligned const specs as final lines — the
    tabwriter alignment math stays in Rust, never here). The blank lines
    are the legacy emission's: one before each enum block, one between
    the type decl and its `const (` group (go/printer's declList rule). -#}// Code generated by Cage — DO NOT EDIT.
// <auto-generated>
//   Generated by Cage — do not edit.
//   schema: {{ schema_hash | default(value="(unavailable)") }}
//   enums:  shared definitions
// </auto-generated>

{{ package_line }}
{% for e in emitted_enums %}
// {{ e.name }}{% if e.description %} — {{ e.description }}{% endif %}
type {{ e.ident }} {{ e.backing }}

const (
{% for l in e.const_lines %}{{ l }}
{% endfor %})
{% endfor %}